Phase 10 — hoist cv::BFMatcher construction out of the per-keypoint matching loops.

Behaviour-preserving: the matcher's two ctor arguments (norm type and crossCheck) are
loop-invariant. `descriptors` is allocated once before the loop
(RegistrationVis.cpp:1104 / :1243 `cv::Mat descriptors(10, descriptorsTo.cols, descriptorsTo.type());`)
so `descriptors.type()` is fixed, and `_nnType` is a member set in parseParameters.

Currently the matcher is constructed once per keypoint. With ~1000-1500 projected
keypoints per frame at 640x480 that is 1000-1500 constructions (each doing an
allocation and a cv::Ptr<BFMatcherImpl> create) per odometry frame.

Estimated saving: 0.2-0.8 ms/frame. Accuracy impact: none.

Apply to: rtabmap_ws/src/rtabmap/corelib/src/RegistrationVis.cpp

